{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"2ca05386d3620102","type":"group","x":-460,"y":-150,"width":940,"height":1020,"label":"Attribution Engine"},
		{"id":"d11d84d0f74b4247","type":"group","x":570,"y":-240,"width":375,"height":1180,"label":"Data Formats "},
		{"id":"88462a2e6772106e","type":"text","text":"Parser(v1):  Data outputs received from EDR Imaging tools like Bosch CDR, Telematic Imaging Tools like Berla iVE, or even CAN logs from tools like CANdump and Wireshark(With Socket Disector)","x":-279,"y":-400,"width":370,"height":143,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"d97397682487f323","type":"text","text":"Hasher(v2)\nA small program that hashes the file in MD5 and SHA-256 formats, to ensure integrity and non-repudiation of the file being sent to the parser. It is the first module to run before the parser begins.","x":-279,"y":-680,"width":370,"height":150,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"8dbc53fb02177aa7","type":"text","text":"Structural Implementation","x":-219,"y":-840,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"#4046a0"},
		{"id":"acd0791e03e03a29","type":"text","text":"Compartmentalization: Every block would be build as a module or a compartment. This is to make debugging, and fixing software bugs for updates during production easier. Also, its to improve it's integrity, especially in the Normalization into the PiF schema block/layer. This enables anyone to look into the inner workings of the schema, in case the issue of the admissibility of iLy is brought into question.","x":-1240,"y":-455,"width":541,"height":175,"color":"#318178"},
		{"id":"51b2aca9d7bdf802","type":"text","text":"Requirements/ Thought Process","x":-1400,"y":-740,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"42096a0248bd2a34","type":"text","text":"Core Languages: C++\n","x":-1720,"y":-455,"width":250,"height":68,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"1201bf032a20d208","type":"text","text":"In the advent of possible issues like  slightly different timestamps of forensic tools, the engine automatically moves to IoC Matching and gives it an \"INCONCLUSIVE DUE TO UNMATCHING RESULTS\"","x":-1061,"y":-110,"width":382,"height":140,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"d4b6e3c209c47f70","type":"text","text":"In the issue of evidence ambiguity or insufficient data, the engine would \n(i) Still look at the data, however would not assign any confidence vector. However, the timeline presentation would serve as a second layer of \"advice\" to the expert, guiding him on where to look to identify cause of attribution.\n(ii) On the account of insufficient data, the engine says its inconclusive","x":-1040,"y":225,"width":341,"height":249,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"227d06aa2ede9d34","type":"text","text":"Attribution Engine(v1): The main engine responsible for determining , based on the timeline presentation the anomalies or IoC's for the IoC Matching layer","x":-269,"y":140,"width":350,"height":170,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"1ce1a969cef91b67","type":"text","text":"TimeLine Construction(v1): After the  schema is done with the normalization, timeline construction begins , as part of the attribution engine. This makes it easier for the attribution engine to attribute a primary and secondary factor to it.","x":-276,"y":-120,"width":363,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"500266ac24bd1559","type":"text","text":"Tagger(v2)\nThe engine tags the file with the engine version, to inform the forensics expert on which policy rules was use to conclude the cause of attribution of the particular incident","x":160,"y":285,"width":320,"height":164,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"183886ae6dd537a2","type":"text","text":"**Normalization With Internal Schema**(v1)\nThe Data received from the parser is converted to the Pi-Format, a unified format for easy digestion by the attribution engine.","x":180,"y":-40,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"f9ec22a839b4d4e5","type":"text","text":"IoC Matching(v1): A group of policies based on a set of rules, which is used to identify the independent root causes or dependent causes(effects) or primary and contributing factors. Example, because of x and y, these are the primary and contributing factors. ","x":-269,"y":414,"width":350,"height":188,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"db84442816921709","type":"text","text":"Timeline Presentation\nThe timeline is constructed and presented in a Markdown File Format.(md), which groups events into compartments for easy follow up and identification Also, a confidence vector would be added to guide the forensics expert in cases where there is insufficient evidence(For example, manual cars cannot collect and store weather data),or possibly ambiguous data with no clear primary and contributing factor ","x":-269,"y":700,"width":350,"height":170,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"7b00aba4d68b625e","type":"text","text":"Maybe we could use the timestamps, not as a threshold for accuracy(It's not going to be used in the court of law), but as a guide for the expert to understand and relate to turn of events","x":-1280,"y":1260,"width":520,"height":180,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"716df95a81d84ba6","type":"text","text":"Suggestions And Errors","x":-1145,"y":1010,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"#d49816"},
		{"id":"0b92dc2b294d7b6c","type":"text","text":"A crucial problem I have identified while looking through Borsh CDR is that, the EDR data it collects varies from car to car.","x":-1192,"y":1600,"width":344,"height":124,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"1821fc554b8d42f1","type":"text","text":"I suggest when you raise points, you leave em to me to figure out the answers","x":-502,"y":1414,"width":342,"height":106,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"514d2b21313fbfa0","type":"text","text":"PiF(Project iLy Format): A unified data schema that gathers all the data from separate sources(EDR, telematics, CAN and ECU data)","x":570,"y":205,"width":290,"height":159},
		{"id":"71f326d1c8ee5ce9","type":"text","text":"Markdown File Format","x":590,"y":573,"width":250,"height":57},
		{"id":"6e834a28a2a242f4","type":"text","text":"Rich Text Format / ODF","x":590,"y":840,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"5082b23dbd56ee3f","type":"text","text":"CSV's,PDF,JSON,PCAP,CANDUMP-FILES","x":590,"y":-180,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"8011d6878654b997","type":"text","text":"Documentation(v1): After everything, it generates a report based on the outputs of the attribution engine. Most likely to be based in an RTF(Rich Text Format) or ODF.","x":-219,"y":1040,"width":250,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"d851208117d0f35e","type":"text","text":"Side Notes\n\nTimeline Construction: After the attribution engine completes its IoC matching, it begins to construct a timeline, this time not just focusing on finding root causes or effects, but then joining pieces to form a series of connected events, known as a timeline. In the absence of adequate evidence for, it becomes the second layer for attribution. Here, ","x":1160,"y":900,"width":560,"height":280},
		{"id":"61fbdeb652479643","type":"text","text":"Sub-languages: \nPython(Digital Twin Simulation)\nMarkdown(Engine)","x":-1785,"y":-289,"width":380,"height":109,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"2dc5cad40e852a47","x":-2204,"y":468,"width":724,"height":352,"type":"text","text":"PiF Event\n├── Core (same for every event, every source)\n│   ├── event_id\n│   ├── timestamp (normalized, e.g. UTC epoch)\n│   ├── source_type        // \"bosch_cdr\" | \"berla_ive\" | \"can_log\"\n│   ├── source_file         // original file this came from\n│   └── raw_reference       // pointer/offset back to the original line/record, for traceability\n│\n└── Payload (source-specific, only one populated per event)\n    ├── CDRPayload      { pre_crash_speed, delta_v, brake_status, ... }\n    ├── iVePayload      { infotainment_event, gps_coord, device_paired, ... }\n    └── CANPayload      { arbitration_id, dlc, data_bytes[], bus_channel }"},
		{"id":"3cc50889b02b3278","x":-1967,"y":320,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Parser Design"},
		{"id":"d4cd0c269c8bfbe3","x":-1720,"y":-79,"width":250,"height":109,"type":"text","text":"Supported Platforms: \nLinux(all debian - v1)\nWindows(v2)\nMaC(v3)\nPlugin for vehicle forensic tools(v4)\n"},
		{"id":"fd2f8f78259a4c83","x":-3020,"y":420,"width":660,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"Timeline (Timeline Construction output)\n├── Core\n│   ├── timeline_id\n│   ├── incident_window        // {start_ts, end_ts} bounding the whole event\n│   ├── anchor_points[]         // list of {event_id, anchor_type, confidence} used to align sources\n│   └── alignment_method        // \"anchored\" | \"tolerance_band_fallback\"\n│\n└── ordered_events[]\n    └── TimelineEvent\n        ├── pif_event           // the original PiF Event, unmodified\n        ├── sequence_index      // position in the resolved order\n        ├── adjusted_timestamp  // post-reconciliation timestamp\n        └── time_confidence     // how sure we are this ordering is correct (high/med/low)"},
		{"id":"f2b5e04cbbe62de4","x":-2815,"y":320,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Timeline Construtction"},
		{"id":"165f3cfe86de4001","x":-3020,"y":1060,"width":675,"height":380,"type":"text","text":"IoC-Annotated Timeline (IoC Matcher output)\n├── Core\n│   ├── same Timeline as above, unmodified (composition, not mutation)\n│\n└── annotations[]\n    └── IoCMatch\n        ├── event_id             // which TimelineEvent this attaches to\n        ├── ioc_id                // reference into your signature/pattern registry\n        ├── ioc_category          // \"cyber\" | \"mechanical\" | \"environmental\" | \"software\"\n        ├── match_type            // \"exact\" | \"pattern\" | \"heuristic\"\n        ├── description           // human-readable, e.g. \"known brake-spoof signature\"\n        └── match_confidence      // per-match confidence, feeds into policy_evaluator's scoring"},
		{"id":"036890b08e5f730b","x":-2139,"y":1060,"width":661,"height":380,"type":"text","text":"Attribution Result (Policy Evaluator / Attribution Engine output)\n├── Core\n│   ├── attribution_id\n│   ├── incident_id            // ties back to the Timeline\n│   └── generated_at\n│\n├── category_scores\n│   ├── cyber            { score, corroboration_tier, contributing_matches[] }\n│   ├── mechanical        { score, corroboration_tier, contributing_matches[] }\n│   ├── environmental     { score, corroboration_tier, contributing_matches[] }\n│   └── software          { score, corroboration_tier, contributing_matches[] }\n│\n└── primary_attribution\n    ├── category            // highest-scoring category\n    ├── confidence          // normalized confidence vector value\n    └── corroboration_tier  // \"high\" | \"medium\" | \"low\" — from your tiered corroboration flagging design"},
		{"id":"b783102575746752","x":-2528,"y":1640,"width":777,"height":340,"type":"text","text":"Presentation Report (Timeline Presentation output)\n├── Core\n│   ├── report_id\n│   ├── source_attribution      // the full AttributionResult, embedded\n│   └── format                  // \"markdown\" | (future: \"pdf\", \"html\")\n│\n└── sections[]\n    ├── summary                 // primary_attribution rendered in plain language\n    ├── timeline_narrative      // ordered_events rendered as a readable sequence\n    ├── evidence_appendix       // raw PiF Events + IoC matches, for audit trail\n    └── confidence_notes        // explanation of corroboration_tier and any low-confidence caveats"},
		{"id":"501efcb1de68e171","x":-1933,"y":950,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Attribution Engine"},
		{"id":"ae61550440cc86f9","x":-2264,"y":1520,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Timeline Presentation"},
		{"id":"1d75eae364017ec8","x":-2840,"y":920,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"IoC Matching"}
	],
